# Purpose of This Guide

This guide explains how to establish, operate, and continuously improve the reporting, KPI, and audit systems required for every Palestine House location.

Reporting and performance measurement are not administrative tasks.

They are the governance systems that:

- Measure mission delivery
- Monitor community impact
- Assess financial sustainability
- Demonstrate operational quality
- Enable HQ to support the network effectively

A location that does not measure performance cannot improve it.

A location that does not report accurately cannot be effectively supported.

Use this guide:

- During location setup
- Before reporting deadlines
- When KPI performance declines
- During HQ audit preparation
- Before annual submissions

---

# Who This Guide Is For

This guide is intended for:

- House Manager
- Finance / Operations Lead
- Board members responsible for governance and performance

Although the House Manager leads reporting, every staff member contributes data through:

- Delivering programmes
- Processing transactions
- Serving guests
- Managing memberships
- Maintaining records

Everyone should understand:

- What is measured
- Why it is measured
- How the information supports Palestine House

---

# Step 1 — Understand the Palestine House KPI Framework

Every Palestine House location operates against a standard KPI Framework defined by HQ.

Performance is measured across five domains.

Each location is expected to report against every domain from its first complete month of operation.

---

# Domain 1 — Community Reach & Programme Delivery

| KPI | Target | Frequency | Data Source | Owner |
|------|--------|-----------|-------------|-------|
| Total unique guests | HQ target by location tier | Monthly | Ticketing & Event Log | House Manager |
| Programme events delivered | Minimum 4 per month | Monthly | Programme Calendar | House Manager |
| Programme diversity | Minimum 3 of 5 cultural pillars each quarter | Quarterly | Programme Review | House Manager |
| Community attendance rate | HQ agreed target | Monthly | Guest Registration | House Manager |

### Cultural Pillars

- P1 — Memory
- P2 — Language
- P3 — Arts
- P4 — Community
- P5 — Learning

---

# Domain 2 — Membership & Community Engagement

| KPI | Target | Frequency | Data Source | Owner |
|------|--------|-----------|-------------|-------|
| Active members | Annual Plan target | Monthly | CRM | Finance/Ops Lead |
| New member growth | Annual Plan target | Monthly | CRM | Finance/Ops Lead |
| Membership renewal | Minimum 70% | Quarterly | CRM | Finance/Ops Lead |
| Member satisfaction | Minimum 4.0 / 5.0 | Quarterly | Member Survey | House Manager |

---

# Domain 3 — Financial Performance

| KPI | Target | Frequency | Data Source | Owner |
|------|--------|-----------|-------------|-------|
| Revenue vs Plan | Within ±10% | Monthly | Finance Report | Finance/Ops Lead |
| Operating surplus | Annual Plan target | Monthly | Finance Report | Finance/Ops Lead |
| Reserve balance | Minimum 3 months fixed costs | Monthly | Reserve Account | Finance/Ops Lead |
| Revenue diversification | No stream above 60% | Quarterly | Business Model Review | Finance/Ops Lead |
| Grant pipeline | Minimum 1 active application | Quarterly | Grant Register | House Manager |

---

# Domain 4 — Operational Quality

| KPI | Target | Frequency | Data Source | Owner |
|------|--------|-----------|-------------|-------|
| HQ reporting on time | 100% | Monthly | Submission Log | House Manager |
| Financial control failures | Zero unresolved | Monthly | Controls Failure Log | Finance/Ops Lead |
| Staff training | 100% completion | As required | Training Register | House Manager |
| Complaint resolution | 100% within 5 working days | Monthly | Complaints Log | House Manager |

---

# Domain 5 — Brand & Governance

| KPI | Target | Frequency | Data Source | Owner |
|------|--------|-----------|-------------|-------|
| HQ approval compliance | 100% | Monthly | Brand Log | House Manager |
| Board meetings | Minimum quarterly | Quarterly | Board Minutes | Board Chair |
| Annual audit | Completed on time | Annual | Auditor Report | Finance/Ops Lead |
