# What This Guide Covers

Catering extends the Palestine House culinary identity beyond the café.

Private events and culinary programmes provide opportunities to share Palestinian culture through food, hospitality, and education while maintaining operational discipline.

This guide explains how to:

- Define the catering identity
- Build standard packages
- Qualify enquiries
- Prepare proposals and quotations
- Confirm bookings correctly
- Plan production
- Protect food safety and allergen communication
- Deliver educational culinary programmes
- Reconcile every event
- Continuously improve the overall offer

Every catered dish continues to follow the **Menu & Palestinian Culinary Identity** process, beverages remain governed by the **Coffee, Tea & Beverage Program**, events follow **Event Production SOPs (Focus Area 4)**, and food safety remains under **Food & Beverage Operations (Focus Area 6).**

---

# Catering, Private Events & Culinary Programming Lifecycle

| Stage | Operational Focus |
|------:|-------------------|
| **1** | Catering Identity |
| **2** | Package Architecture |
| **3** | Enquiry & Qualification |
| **4** | Proposal & Quote |
| **5** | Confirmation & Deposit |
