# Purpose

Global campaigns are among the most visible activities undertaken across the Palestine House network.

Their success depends on every location communicating with:

- Consistent messaging
- Coordinated timing
- Approved brand assets
- Non-political positioning
- HQ alignment

This guide identifies the most common operational failures that can weaken campaign effectiveness, create legal or reputational risk, or compromise the integrity of the Palestine House network.

Each Risk Card includes:

- **What the issue looks like**
- **Why it matters**
- **Required response**
- **Mandatory escalation trigger**

> **Important**
>
> Whenever uncertainty exists, escalate to HQ.
>
> Palestine House would rather receive an unnecessary escalation than discover a campaign failure through the media, partners, or the public.

---

# Global Campaign Lifecycle

| Stage | Operational Area |
|------:|------------------|
| **1** | Campaign Brief |
| **2** | Content & Creative |
| **3** | HQ Approval |
| **4** | Local Activation |
| **5** | Live Execution |
| **6** | Monitoring & Response |
| **7** | Report & Review |

