# Section 1 — Common Mistakes

Operational failures that undermine campaign quality and network alignment.

---

# Risk Card 01

## Common Mistake

### Activating a Global Campaign Before Reviewing the Local Execution Brief

---

### What It Looks Like

A local Palestine House receives campaign assets from HQ and immediately begins:

- Publishing content
- Scheduling posts
- Creating local adaptations
- Promoting the campaign

without first reviewing the Local Execution Brief.

---

### Why It Matters

Global campaigns depend on network coordination.

Publishing too early, out of sequence, or without required campaign elements can:

- Break campaign timing
- Reduce network impact
- Contradict coordinated messaging
- Undermine HQ planning
- Create inconsistency across locations

---

### Required Action

Before publishing any campaign material:

- Request the Local Execution Brief
- Review campaign objectives
- Confirm launch timing
- Understand mandatory assets
- Understand optional assets
- Confirm approved local adaptations
- Review reporting requirements

If no brief has been received within **five working days** after campaign assets arrive, contact HQ before proceeding.

---

### Escalate Immediately If

- Campaign content has been published before the HQ launch date.
- Campaign content has been published before the Local Execution Brief has been reviewed.

If this occurs:

1. Remove the content immediately.
2. Notify HQ without delay.

---

# Risk Card 02

## Common Mistake

### Adapting Campaign Messaging Without HQ Approval

---

### What It Looks Like

The local team modifies HQ messaging to make it feel:

- More local
- More culturally familiar
- Better translated
- More engaging

without submitting the changes to HQ.

---

### Why It Matters

HQ messaging has already been reviewed for:

- Cultural sensitivity
- Political neutrality
- Legal risk
- Brand consistency
- Narrative sequencing

Even well-intentioned local changes may:

- Introduce political language
- Change campaign meaning
- Create inconsistencies
- Conflict with other locations

---

### Required Action

If adaptation is necessary:

Submit to HQ:

- Original message
- Proposed revision
- Reason for change
- Intended audience

Do not publish until written approval is received.

If approval cannot be obtained before launch, use the approved HQ version.

---

### Escalate Immediately If

A modified message has already been published and:

- Contains political language
- Departs from HQ messaging
- Makes claims not approved by HQ

Provide HQ with:

- Screenshot
- Description of the modification
- Publication details

---

# Risk Card 03

## Common Mistake

### Using Campaign Assets Outside Their Approved Purpose

---

### What It Looks Like

Examples include:

- Instagram graphics used in newsletters
- Posters reused as social media artwork
- Organic videos used in paid advertising
- Assets resized for unapproved channels

---

### Why It Matters

Campaign assets are created and licensed for specific uses.

Misuse may create:

- Poor presentation quality
- Brand inconsistency
- Copyright issues
- Licensing violations
- Legal exposure

---

### Required Action

Only use campaign assets:

- On approved channels
- At approved sizes
- For approved purposes

If another version is required:

Request the correct asset from HQ.

Before using any campaign video in paid advertising, obtain written licence confirmation.

---

### Escalate Immediately If

Campaign assets have been used:

- In paid advertising
- In broadcast media
- Outside approved territories
- Beyond the original licence

HQ must immediately review licensing.

---

# Section 2 — Risks

Structural risks affecting campaign integrity.

---

# Risk Card 04

## Risk

### Campaign Timing Becomes Misaligned Across Locations

---

### What It Looks Like

Different Houses publish:

- Early
- Late
- Out of sequence

creating multiple campaign stages simultaneously.

---

### Why It Matters

Global campaigns rely upon synchronised communication.

Timing failures reduce:

- Network impact
- Brand consistency
- Public clarity
- Media effectiveness

---

### Required Action

Treat campaign launch dates as fixed commitments.

Immediately assess whether:

- Translation
- Scheduling
- Local preparation

can be completed before launch.

If not, notify HQ immediately.

Never launch early.

Never delay without informing HQ.

---

### Escalate Immediately If

A location:

- Misses launch by more than 24 hours
- Publishes out-of-sequence campaign content

HQ will determine whether corrective synchronisation is required.

---

# Risk Card 05

## Risk

### Community Responses Become Political

---

### What It Looks Like

A staff member responds to campaign comments with personal political opinions from an official Palestine House account.

The response is then shared publicly as the institutional position of Palestine House.

---

### Why It Matters

Campaigns generate significant public engagement.

Any response published from an official account becomes:

- The perceived institutional position
- A potential media story
- A reputational risk

---

### Required Action

Prepare response protocols before launch.

Include:

- Approved response wording
- Escalation topics
- House Manager approval requirements
- HQ escalation process

Never publish political responses without written HQ approval.

---

### Escalate Immediately If

A campaign response:

- Has been screenshotted
- Has gone viral
- Has been quoted publicly
- Has been reported as a Palestine House political statement

Notify HQ immediately.

Do not delete content without HQ direction.

---

# Risk Card 06

## Risk

### Campaign Partnerships Created Without Political Screening

---

### What It Looks Like

A community organisation offers to amplify the campaign.

The local House accepts without reviewing:

- Political affiliations
- Advocacy activities
- Reputational concerns

---

### Why It Matters

Campaign partners are publicly associated with Palestine House.

A politically affiliated partner may create the appearance of endorsement.

---

### Required Action

Before accepting campaign partnerships:

Review:

- Political affiliations
- Advocacy activity
- Previous HQ assessments

If uncertain:

Submit the organisation to HQ.

Do not publicly acknowledge campaign partners before approval.

---

### Escalate Immediately If

A campaign partner is discovered to have:

- Political party affiliations
- Advocacy positions inconsistent with Palestine House principles

Notify HQ immediately.

Await guidance before making any public response.

---

# Section 3 — Red Flags

Situations requiring immediate action.

---

# Risk Card 07

## Red Flag

### Campaign Content Contains Political Language or Imagery

---

### What It Looks Like

Campaign content contains:

- Political slogans
- Political hashtags
- Politically sensitive maps
- Politically affiliated public figures
- Language implying political positions

---

### Why It Matters

Even implied political messaging may:

- Damage Palestine House positioning
- Create legal issues
- Generate controversy
- Remain permanently visible through screenshots

---

### Required Action

Immediately:

1. Remove the content.
2. Notify HQ within one hour.
3. Provide:
   - Screenshot
   - Publication time
   - Estimated reach
   - Description of the issue

Do not publish corrections without HQ approval.

---

### Escalate Immediately If

The content has already been:

- Shared
- Screenshotted
- Covered by media

HQ will determine the response.

---

# Risk Card 08

## Red Flag

### Campaign Generates Media Questions Beyond Local Authority

---

### What It Looks Like

Journalists request comments regarding:

- Political implications
- Funding
- Palestine House positions
- Campaign objectives

Local representatives answer without HQ involvement.

---

### Why It Matters

Media interviews may quickly become political.

Poorly prepared responses can become national headlines.

---

### Required Action

Respond only with:

> "Thank you for your enquiry. I will connect you with the appropriate person to provide a full response."

Then immediately notify HQ with:

- Journalist name
- Publication
- Questions received
- Deadline

---

### Escalate Immediately If

A representative has already:

- Spoken to media
- Given quotations
- Agreed to interviews

HQ should be notified before publication whenever possible.

---

# Section 4 — Compliance Issues

Breaches of campaign reporting requirements.

---

# Risk Card 09

## Compliance Issue

### Campaign Performance Data Not Reported to HQ

---

### What It Looks Like

Campaign reporting is:

- Late
- Incomplete
- Missing
- Poorly tracked

---

### Why It Matters

HQ requires campaign reporting for:

- Network evaluation
- Future planning
- Funder reporting
- Partner reporting

Repeated failures reduce network effectiveness.

---

### Required Action

Before campaign launch:

Confirm:

- Required KPIs
- Reporting format
- Submission deadline
- Reporting owner

If delays occur, notify HQ before the deadline.

---

### Escalate Immediately If

The House has:

- Missed two consecutive reporting deadlines
- Submitted unreliable campaign data

HQ may require:

- Corrective reporting plans
- Formal review
- Tracking improvements

---

# Section 5 — Escalation Triggers

Situations requiring immediate HQ leadership.

---

# Risk Card 10

## Escalation Trigger

### A Global Campaign Creates a Public Crisis

---

### What It Looks Like

Examples include:

- Community backlash
- Media controversy
- Platform restrictions
- Public criticism
- Partner complaints
- Government enquiries
- Funder concerns

---

### Why It Matters

A local crisis quickly becomes a network issue.

Only HQ can coordinate:

- Media responses
- Campaign changes
- Network messaging
- Crisis communications

---

### Required Action

Immediately:

1. Pause all campaign publishing.
2. Do not remove existing content unless instructed.
3. Contact HQ within **30 minutes**.
4. Send supporting information, including:
   - Screenshots
   - Links
   - Media coverage
   - Community reactions
   - Organisations involved

Do not make any public statement until HQ provides written direction.

---

### Escalate Immediately If

Any of the following occur:

- Media describes Palestine House as a political organisation
- Campaign content is removed or restricted by a platform
- Coordinated public attacks occur
- Complaints are received from:
  - Funders
  - Government agencies
  - Institutional partners
- Prominent public figures publicly criticise the campaign on political grounds

HQ assumes command.

The local House provides support but does not lead communications.

---

# Note for House Managers

Global campaigns are the moments when Palestine House speaks most visibly to the world.

They require:

- Discipline
- Coordination
- Consistency
- Careful review
- Early escalation

The Local Execution Brief exists to protect every House—not to restrict local creativity.

Whenever uncertainty exists:

- Check before publishing.
- Ask before adapting.
- Escalate before responding.
- Report when complete.

HQ is your partner—not your auditor.

Early communication prevents larger problems later.

