## 10. Global Campaign Creates a Public Crisis

**Category:** Escalation Trigger

### What it looks like

A campaign generates:

- Community backlash
- Political criticism
- Media controversy
- Platform restrictions
- Funder complaints
- Government enquiries
- Organised online campaigns

### Why it matters

Local campaign crises quickly become network crises.

Only HQ can coordinate:

- Media response
- Platform response
- Brand protection
- Network-wide decisions

### What to do

Immediately:

1. Stop publishing campaign content.
2. Do **not** remove existing content unless instructed.
3. Call HQ within **30 minutes**.
4. Send an email containing:
   - Description of the issue
   - Triggering content
   - Screenshots
   - Media links
   - Community reactions
   - Organisations involved

Do not:

- Issue statements
- Reply publicly
- Comment privately on behalf of Palestine House

until HQ provides written direction.

### Escalate if

Any of the following occur:

- Media portrays Palestine House politically.
- Platforms remove or restrict campaign content.
- Organised community or political opposition develops.
- Complaints are received from funders or government.
- Prominent public figures criticise the campaign.

HQ assumes command.

The Local House supports—but does not lead—the response.

---

# A Note for House Managers

Global campaigns represent the moments when Palestine House speaks most visibly to the world.

They are also the moments when the difference between excellence and reputational damage is smallest.

Campaign failures most commonly occur when:

- Local enthusiasm exceeds HQ coordination.
- Campaign messaging is adapted without approval.
- Non-Political positioning is compromised.
- Publishing moves faster than review.

Discipline—not caution—is what protects both the campaign and the people delivering it.

The **Local Execution Brief** is not a limitation on creativity.

It is the framework that allows every Palestine House location to contribute confidently, consistently, and safely to a coordinated global campaign.

> **HQ is your partner—not your auditor.**
>
> Escalate early.
> Ask before adapting.
> Review before publishing.
> Report after completion.

---

**Passion Inspires. Discipline Delivers.**

