# Step 3 — Configure Ticketing, Payments & Financial Controls

Every payment received by Palestine House must use the approved financial infrastructure.

This includes:

- Tickets
- Memberships
- Café sales
- Merchandise
- Venue hire
- Donations

Personal accounts or unapproved payment methods must never be used.

---

## Ticketing Platform

Configure:

- Event categories
- Pricing tiers
- Branding

Complete end-to-end testing before launch.

---

## Payment Gateway

Confirm:

- Approved provider
- Connected bank account
- Tested settlement
- Refund workflow

---

## Accounting Software

Configure:

- Chart of accounts
- Revenue categories
- Payment integration

Restrict access to authorised finance staff.

---

## Financial Controls

Maintain:

- Dual approvals
- Expense workflows
- Monthly reconciliation schedule

---

> **Important**
>
> Every revenue stream must be recorded as a separate income category.
>
> Do not merge revenue streams.

---

## Decision Point

**Have end-to-end payment tests been completed successfully?**

### Yes

Proceed.

### No

Do not accept payments until testing is complete.

---

## Expected Output

- [ ] Ticketing platform tested
- [ ] Payment gateway tested
- [ ] Accounting software configured
- [ ] Financial controls documented

