# What This Guide Covers

The Palestine House Template Library provides the operational foundation for every House across the global network.

This guide explains how to:

- Understand the purpose of the template library
- Access and use the Master Index
- Customise templates appropriately
- Maintain compliance with submission schedules
- Keep templates current
- Contribute improvements back to the network

Templates are not administrative paperwork—they are operational tools that ensure consistency, accountability, and shared standards across every Palestine House location.

---

# Template Library Lifecycle

| Stage | Operational Focus |
|------:|-------------------|
| **1** | Library Setup |
| **2** | Master Index Access |
| **3** | Local Customisation |
| **4** | Active Operations |
| **5** | Compliance Review |
| **6** | Annual Update |
| **7** | Annual Library Review |
| **8** | Continuous Evolution |

---

# Step 1 — Understand the Purpose of the Template Library

The Template Library exists so every Palestine House operates to the same standard.

Templates capture accumulated operational experience and transform it into repeatable processes.

They provide:

- Consistency
- Accountability
- Governance
- Comparable reporting
- Operational discipline

Ignoring templates weakens operational standards.

Using them consistently strengthens the entire network.

---

## Decision Point

**Does every team member know which templates exist, where they are stored, and which ones they are responsible for?**

Before operations begin:

- Introduce the library
- Demonstrate the Master Index
- Assign template ownership
- Confirm access through the Knowledge Management System (KMS)

---

## Expected Output

- [ ] Team briefing completed
- [ ] Master Index accessible
- [ ] Template responsibilities assigned
- [ ] Library orientation documented

---

# Step 2 — Access the Master Index

The Master Index is the single source of truth for every Palestine House template.

It identifies:

- Template location
- Operational category
- Lifecycle stage
- Submission requirements
- Responsible owner

Always check the Master Index before creating a new document.

---

## Template Categories

### Governance & Legal

Includes:

- Sustainability Framework Statement
- Sponsorship Ethics Screening Record
- Board Session Minutes
- Board Resolution Record

---

### Revenue & Membership

Includes:

- Monthly Revenue Report
- Grants & Sponsorship Tracker
- Membership Programme Design

---

### Impact Measurement

Includes:

- Quarterly Impact Report
- Annual Impact Summary
- Impact Evidence Archive

---

### Operations & Improvement

Includes:

- Feedback Infrastructure Map
- Learning Loop Record
- KMS Audit Report
- Monthly Operations Review

---

### Team & Human Resources

Includes:

- Team Development Plan
- Individual Development Plan
- Role Handover Document

---

### Community & Partnerships

Includes:

- Community Deepening Plan
- Partnership Activity Log
- Community Listening Report

---

### Network & Standards

Includes:

- Quarterly Learning Submission
- Standards Update Log
- Annual Network Contribution Plan

---

### Launch Planning

Includes:

- RACI Matrix
- Gate Reports
- Weekly Meeting Log
- Venue Scorecard
- Snagging & Readiness Log

---

## Decision Point

**Does a template already exist for this requirement?**

Always:

1. Check the Master Index.
2. Use existing templates where possible.
3. Follow the approved customisation process if adaptation is required.

Avoid creating duplicate documentation.

---

## Expected Output

- [ ] Master Index available through KMS
- [ ] Template locations confirmed
- [ ] Submission requirements understood
- [ ] Template ownership assigned

---

# Step 3 — Customise Templates Correctly

Templates are designed for use across multiple countries and operational contexts.

Some fields are:

- Fixed (must not change)
- Flexible (may be adapted locally)

---

## Customisation Rules

### Fixed Fields

Never modify without HQ approval.

Examples include:

- Reporting categories
- Standard KPIs
- Core governance fields

---

### Flexible Fields

May be adapted to reflect:

- Local legislation
- Operational context
- Cultural requirements
- Language

---

## Decision Point

**Have all local adaptations been documented and, where necessary, approved by HQ?**

Changes to fixed fields require HQ review before implementation.

---

## Expected Output

- [ ] Local Customisation Log maintained
- [ ] HQ approval obtained where required
- [ ] Adaptations documented
- [ ] Updated versions stored in KMS

---

# Step 4 — Use Mandatory Templates on Schedule

Different templates carry different governance responsibilities.

Some are:

- Mandatory HQ submissions
- Mandatory internal documents
- Recommended operational tools

The House Manager is accountable for every required submission.

---

## Annual Submission Calendar

Maintain a calendar showing:

- Submission deadlines
- Preparation lead times
- Responsible owner
- Review dates

Review quarterly.

---

## Decision Point

**Has the annual submission calendar been confirmed before the operational year begins?**

Proactive scheduling improves quality and reduces compliance risk.

---

## Expected Output

- [ ] Submission calendar completed
- [ ] Owners assigned
- [ ] Preparation timelines confirmed
- [ ] Board review scheduled

---

# Step 5 — Maintain Submission Quality

Every submitted template must contain genuine operational data.

Accuracy is more important than appearance.

---

## Submission Standard

Templates should contain:

- Verified figures
- Honest assessment
- Supporting evidence
- Complete records

Avoid:

- Estimates
- Placeholder text
- Unsupported claims
- Narrative replacing evidence

---

## House Manager Review

Before submission, confirm:

- Accuracy
- Completeness
- Evidence
- Accountability

If additional time is genuinely required, notify HQ proactively.

---

## Decision Point

**Can the House Manager personally confirm the accuracy of every submitted field?**

Only submit documents that accurately reflect operational reality.

---

## Expected Output

- [ ] Actual data used
- [ ] House Manager review completed
- [ ] Supporting evidence archived
- [ ] HQ acknowledgement recorded

---

# Step 6 — Keep the Library Current

Templates require ongoing maintenance.

Version control protects operational consistency.

---

## Version Management

When HQ releases updates:

- Replace outdated versions
- Archive previous versions
- Notify all relevant users
- Update the Master Index

Complete updates within **10 working days**.

---

## Version Control Log

Record:

- HQ release date
- Local update date
- Team notification date
- Archive confirmation

Review during each KMS audit.

---

## Decision Point

**Is there a documented process for replacing outdated templates promptly?**

Strong version control prevents inconsistent operational practices.

---

## Expected Output

- [ ] Version Control Log maintained
- [ ] KMS updated
- [ ] Team notified
- [ ] Previous versions archived

---

# Step 7 — Conduct the Annual Template Review

Review the entire library every year.

The objective is to:

- Align
- Retire
- Improve
- Expand

---

## Annual Review Activities

Confirm:

- HQ alignment
- Obsolete templates retired
- Operational gaps identified
- Requests for new templates submitted

---

## Local Documents

Review locally-created:

- Forms
- Logs
- Trackers
- Reports

Determine whether they should become network standards.

---

## Decision Point

**Are locally-developed templates being shared with HQ for review?**

Every useful innovation should be evaluated for wider network benefit.

---

## Expected Output

- [ ] Annual Template Review completed
- [ ] Alignment confirmed
- [ ] Retired templates documented
- [ ] New template requests submitted
- [ ] HQ review requested

---

# Step 8 — Contribute to the Global Library

Operational improvements should strengthen the entire Palestine House network.

Every mature House should actively contribute to the evolution of the global library.

---

## Submit Contributions

Include:

- Template
- Operational purpose
- Context
- Benefits
- Potential network value

HQ evaluates whether the document should become part of the global standard.

---

## Decision Point

**Has this House created a document that could benefit other Houses?**

If the answer is yes:

Submit it.

HQ will determine whether it should become a global resource.

---

## Expected Output

- [ ] Template contribution submitted
- [ ] Operational context documented
- [ ] Network value explained
- [ ] HQ review requested

---

# Quick Reference

| Step | Action | Owner | Timing |
|------:|--------|-------|--------|
| **1** | Understand Template Library | House Manager | During onboarding |
| **2** | Access Master Index | All Team Members | Before creating documents |
